------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Protocol and interoperability
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

adbc-driver-quack is an independent client for DuckDB's Quack remote protocol
(protocol version 3, as served by DuckDB 2.0's quack extension). The message
and vector formats were implemented by reference to the openly licensed
sources of duckdb/duckdb-quack and duckdb/duckdb (MIT License,
Copyright (c) the DuckDB Foundation): https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb-quack

The binary codec design was ported from gizmodata/quack-jdbc (MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2026 GizmoData LLC), itself clean-room ported from
tobilg/quack-protocol (MIT License): https://github.com/tobilg/quack-protocol

DuckDB is a trademark of the DuckDB Foundation. This project is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by the DuckDB Foundation or DuckDB
Labs.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Apache Arrow ADBC
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

pkg/quack/driver.go, pkg/quack/utils.c, pkg/quack/utils.h and
pkg/quack/adbc.h are generated from, or copied from, the templates and
headers of Apache Arrow ADBC (https://github.com/apache/arrow-adbc), licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). The driver is built on the
arrow-adbc Go framework and the Apache Arrow Go libraries (Apache-2.0).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADBC conformance suite (test only)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

validation/queries/type/select/*.txtcase and validation/queries/ingest/*.txtcase
are DuckDB query overrides from adbc-drivers/quack
(https://github.com/adbc-drivers/quack), Copyright (c) 2026 ADBC Drivers
Contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; they keep their
license headers. The files in validation/queries/type/bind/ are generated by
scripts/gen_validation_overrides.py from the base cases of
adbc-drivers/validation (Apache-2.0). The conformance suite itself
(https://github.com/adbc-drivers/validation) is a test dependency and is not
distributed with this project.
